# Chimera @VERSION@ (alpha)

Alternative firmware for the PreenFM3: a multi-engine, multitimbral digital synth with chain-based navigation. Alpha software for testers: expect rough edges, and keep your stock firmware handy.

Built from source commit `@COMMIT@`, @DATE@.

## What's in

- `chimera-@VERSION@.zip`: the firmware. Unpacked, it holds the two files to install, `chimera-@VERSION@.bin` and `chimera-@VERSION@.bk2`; always install them together.
- `chimera-@redacted`: the same firmware with the ORBIT generative sequencer.
- `chimera-usb.py`: the console tool (Python 3, nothing to install): `python3 chimera-usb.py status` prints the unit's state for a bug report; `shot` saves a screenshot; `put` sends TAPE sources and library Sounds to the card. `python3 chimera-usb.py --help` lists the rest.
- `SHA256SUMS`: check the downloads with `sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS`.

## Install, and roll back

Pick one file, `chimera-@VERSION@.zip` or the `-orbit` one, and update once:

- **With the bootloader:** unpack the zip, put the unit in the bootloader's USB disk mode, delete any older chimera `.bin` and `.bk2` files from the card, drag both new files onto it, and run the bootloader's update. The first start installs the rest behind DON'T POWER OFF: leave it on until it plays.
- **Or with the tool:** with the unit on and connected, `python3 chimera-usb.py update chimera-@VERSION@.zip`. It checks the package, flashes, waits for the first start, and prints `OK updated` when it is done (it needs dfu-util).

The [README](https://github.com/joegiralt/chimera-releases#readme) has the details and the steps to go back to the stock firmware. Never write the bootloader (anything below `0x08020000`) or the option bytes. On the card, Chimera writes only under `/CHIMERA/`; the only file it reads outside it is the `.bk2` you put there, and it never touches your stock files.

